<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Acid Drop</h1>
<p>Sphere: Acid Sphere
Spell Tier: 1
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 100)
Mana: 15
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast acid drop &lt;target&gt;
<a cmd='#'>cast acid drop</a>   (at whoever you are fighting)
</pre>
<p>The caster utters 'Drist causter', and a drop of acid forms above the 
target and falls on them. It is the first and weakest of the acid spells: 
the better your magic and your acid sphere, the more it burns. Acid eats 
through metal, so it does better against chain and plate than against 
clothes and leather, but a shield can block it.
</p><p>Casting it is an attack and starts a fight. It can be cast while fighting, 
and no free hands are needed. It is also found on wands, staffs and 
scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spray of Acid</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Acid Ball</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Acid Swirl</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Acid Resistance</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Acid Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>